      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nFix `compile/fullgraph/test_full_graph.py::test_custom_compile_config[compilation_config3-facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs3]` in CI.  E.g. [main-branch Buildkite run #98732](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/98732/table?jid=01a18d91-e51c-4804-959e-7e5d4fa8bf8d&tab=output).\r\n\r\nFailure was exposed by the [automatic fullgraph sharding PR #64635](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/64635).\r\n\r\nBefore sharding, the test shared a cache with another test that created an AOT artifact. After sharding, it could run alone with a cold cache and expose a pre-existing `depyf`/PyTorch 2.14 incompatibility.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- The cold-cache test no longer fails with `patched_load_by_key_path() got an unexpected keyword argument 'set_sys_modules'`.\r\n- The long-term fix belongs upstream in `depyf`; this is a vLLM compatibility shim until that fix is released.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n```bash\r\naot_cache=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vllm-aot-repro.XXXXXX)\r\nVLLM_CACHE_ROOT=\"$aot_cache\" \\\r\nVLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE=1 \\\r\nVLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=0 \\\r\npytest -s -v \\\r\n  'compile/fullgraph/test_full_graph.py::test_full_graph[facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs0-3]' \\\r\n  'compile/fullgraph/test_full_graph.py::test_custom_compile_config[compilation_config3-facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs3]'\r\n```\r\n\r\nPass on both main and this PR because test_`full_graph[facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs0-3]` created an AOT artifact in the shared cache before `test_custom_compile_config[compilation_config3-facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs3]` ran.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nrepro_cache=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vllm-repro.XXXXXX)\r\nVLLM_CACHE_ROOT=\"$repro_cache\" \\\r\nVLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE=1 \\\r\nVLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=0 \\\r\npytest -s -v \\\r\n  'compile/fullgraph/test_full_graph.py::test_custom_compile_config[compilation_config3-facebook/opt-125m-model_kwargs3]'\r\n```\r\n\r\nFails on main with `torch._inductor.exc.InductorError: RuntimeError: Failed to run autotuning code block: patched_load_by_key_path() got an unexpected keyword argument 'set_sys_modules'`. Passes on this branch.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n`depyf==0.20.0` patches Torch Inductor's `PyCodeCache.load_by_key_path` but does not accept PyTorch 2.14's new `set_sys_modules` keyword. The compatibility shim adds the keyword to the patched wrapper and forwards it to Torch's original loader while preserving depyf's source dumping.\r\n\r\nThe cleanest permanent fix is to update depyf's wrapper and then bump vLLM's depyf dependency and remove the shim.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
